    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s lineup for May 5th centers on capitalizing against soft-tossing right-handed starters, with **Bryson Stott** (72.46) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (71.77) leading the charge as our strongest plays. **Bryson Stott** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Severino and helpful wind conditions, while **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a staple at the #3 hole, maintaining an elite efficiency score despite the high-leverage nature of his opponent. **Matt Chapman** (70.02) rounds out our top trio, thriving against the porous xERA of Walker Buehler. We are specifically leveraging \"Slow SP Delivery\" metrics against Buehler, which provides a massive boost to the stolen base upside for **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Daulton Varsho**, and **Drew Gilbert**, who are all positioned to exploit the battery\u2019s inability to control the running game.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Gavin Sheets** (42.40), who sat on the bubble of our UTIL slot. While he offers a decent platoon edge against the right-handed Webb, the SP skill variance of a 3.30 xERA made him too risky compared to the higher-floor options locked in our starting nine. **Wenceel Perez** (66.93) proved to be a high-value play; despite a lower base projection, he surged into our active lineup due to a substantial 11% platoon boost and favorable wind factors. Note that we are monitoring **Tyler Freeman** closely due to a confirmed rainout, ensuring he remains benched to protect our limited game-cap pool. **Cal Raleigh**, **Will Smith**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Taylor Ward**, **Lawrence Butler**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Luis Arraez**, **Masyn Winn**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, and **Gleyber Torres** round out the remaining depth considerations, though we remain cautious of the tough assignments faced by **Will Smith** and **Jonathan Aranda** against sub-4.00 xERA arms.",
